'''''Bellis pappulosa''''' is a species of daisy in the genus ''[[Bellis]]''. This species is native in Western Europe, Algeria, France, Morocco and Spain.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:184404-1|title=''Bellis pappulosa'' <small>Boiss.</small> ex DC. &#124; Plants of the World Online &#124; Kew Science|website=Plants of the World Online}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://identify.plantnet.org/weurope/species/Bellis%20pappulosa%20Boiss./data|title=''Bellis pappulosa'' <small>Boiss.</small> (Western Europe) - Pl@ntNet identify}}</ref>

''B. pappulosa'' is morphologically similar to ''[[Bellis sylvestris]]'' but has scales on the [[Pappus (botany)|pappus]] of the seeds, which are absent in ''B. sylvestris''.<ref>{{cite journal |last1=Calvo |first1=J. |last2=Quintanar |first2=A. |last3=Aedo |first3=C. |title=Typification of four species names of ''Bellis'' (Compositae) |journal=Nordic Journal of Botany |date=2012 |volume=30 |pages=668–670 |doi=10.1111/j.1756-1051.2012.01373.x}}</ref> Moreover, ''B. pappulosa'' is [[diploid]] while ''B. sylvestris'' is [[polyploid]].<ref>{{cite journal |last1=Fiz |first1=O. |last2=Valcárcel |first2=V. |last3=Vargas |first3=P. |title=Phylogenetic position of Mediterranean Astereae and character evolution of daisies (''Bellis'', Asteraceae) inferred from nrDNA ITS sequences |journal=Molecular Phylogenetics and Evolution |date=2002 |volume=25 |pages=157–171 |doi=10.1016/S1055-7903(02)00228-2}}</ref> 

